{
  "id": 447645800,
  "iid": 23294,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Lua: Free func savers when resetting thread",
  "description": "Unlike everything else that is allocated and freed with the\nclear_outstanding_ functions, the FuncSavers are stored directly\nin the lua_State. That means that they need to be freed before\nthe lua_State thread is reset, not at the end of the packet_info.\n\nUse g_ptr_array_new_with_free_func to simplify things a bit.\n\nFixup eb2a59a3628c52a53b1e2eeba38d1a5f412101d7\n\nFix #20963. (In reality, this has been broken and was already\ncommitting an illegal access, but certain details of the garbage\ncollection and memory allocation somehow allowed the test to pass\nanyway except when more enums were added and thus more memory used\nby each lua_State.)\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-01-20T03:10:42.357Z",
